{"uid":"d1c0ae43bf868663","name":"test_both_peer_gates_compose_in_one_run","fullName":"tests.flows.test_flow_peer_gates#test_both_peer_gates_compose_in_one_run","historyId":"8b88f75acdae16421600adff5a91517c","time":{"start":1791935289526,"stop":1791935291712,"duration":2186},"description":"`peer_plan_review: true` + `peer_verdict_gate: true`, non-vigilant,\n    with BOTH gates driven through a real round trip in the same run: the\n    first `plan_review` invocation objects (spending approach 1's one\n    revision) and the second approves; then, after `review` verifies, the\n    `verdict_gate` invocation REJECTS carrying a genuinely non-curable\n    blocking finding (the stub's `STUB_VERDICT_GATE_REJECT_COUNT` knob,\n    same shape `test_a_verdict_gate_rejection_with_a_non_curable_finding_\n    ends_the_run_even_with_an_approach_left` drives alone). v0.21.1\n    requirement A (task 001) means that rejection ends the run failed/\n    unverified RIGHT THERE, even with `max_approaches=2` leaving a second\n    approach available -- no archive, no fresh approach, no second\n    `verdict_gate` invocation. This is the composition `tests/test_e2e_\n    composed_gates_task032.py::test_both_peer_gates_enabled_in_the_same_\n    run` used to own (task 020, C.9), updated for requirement A: both\n    gates are still observably exercised for real (plan_review's full\n    objection-then-approval round trip, verdict_gate's real rejection),\n    just never reaching a second approach now that the rejection itself\n    ends the run instead of spending one.","descriptionHtml":"<p><code>peer_plan_review: true</code> + <code>peer_verdict_gate: true</code>, non-vigilant,<br />\nwith BOTH gates driven through a real round trip in the same run: the<br />\nfirst <code>plan_review</code> invocation objects (spending approach 1's one<br />\nrevision) and the second approves; then, after <code>review</code> verifies, the<br />\n<code>verdict_gate</code> invocation REJECTS carrying a genuinely non-curable<br />\nblocking finding (the stub's <code>STUB_VERDICT_GATE_REJECT_COUNT</code> knob,<br />\nsame shape <code>test_a_verdict_gate_rejection_with_a_non_curable_finding_ ends_the_run_even_with_an_approach_left</code> drives alone). v0.21.1<br />\nrequirement A (task 001) means that rejection ends the run failed/<br />\nunverified RIGHT THERE, even with <code>max_approaches=2</code> leaving a second<br />\napproach available -- no archive, no fresh approach, no second<br />\n<code>verdict_gate</code> invocation. This is the composition <code>tests/test_e2e_ composed_gates_task032.py::test_both_peer_gates_enabled_in_the_same_ run</code> used to own (task 020, C.9), updated for requirement A: both<br />\ngates are still observably exercised for real (plan_review's full<br />\nobjection-then-approval round trip, verdict_gate's real rejection),<br />\njust never reaching a second approach now that the rejection itself<br />\nends the run instead of spending one.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791935289468,"stop":1791935289486,"duration":18},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791935289468,"stop":1791935289468,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791935289487,"stop":1791935289487,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_scrub_notifier_env_in_process","time":{"sta